Deck - reffers to the player's current cards
In Play - reffers to cards on the board/in play
Pile - reffers to cards in the sack; place cards are to be drawn from
Pack - reffers to the set of tiles in play in a row
Place - placing a pack or adding to an established pack
Throw Out - removing a card from your deck into the draw pile, signifying the end of your turn
Pick Up - picking up a card from the draw pile adding to your deck, signifying the begninning of your turn
Board - where the packs are placed



There are 106 tiles: 2 jokers + 2 sets of each (4) colours (totaling to 8) sets of 1-13 (2 sets of red (26), 2 sets of blue (26),
2 sets of orange (26), 2 sets of black (26))

Colours are 'Black, Blue, Orange, Red'

The joker represents any tile, regardless of colour or value is is any tile

The game is started by all players picking up from the draw pile. the player with the highest value begins (a joker is the highest,
imagine it as 14) and is then decided clockwise from the begining player



Rules:



- Packs must have a length of 3 or greater



- The sets loop meaning that a 1 can be placed after a 13 so that packs such as '12 13 1' are valid



- Packs can be made either by being of the same colour or of the same number
   The 'colour packs' numbers must be consecutive, meaning the pack must be as shown: [4, 5, 6], [11, 12, 13, 1], not: [2, 4, 7]
   The 'same number packs' must not repeat the same colour, meaning that [orange, red, blue] is valid, but [black blue red black]
   is not; one black can be removed and it becomes valid



- You cannot place a deck onto the board on your first turn



- You cannot add to an established pack or change other packs before placing down a pack of your own



- You can change packs already placed, for example if you have a {black 3} and {black 4}, and there is a pack on the board with a 
  [black 5, black 6, black 7, black 8], you can take the {5} and place down your {black 3} and {black 4} alongside it to make 
  [black 3, 4, 5]



- When a pack is changed, it must still be valid so no packs less than 3 or with unconsecutive numbers

   This means you can also split packs. eg: you have {black 5}, on board: [black 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7]. you can split it into [2, 3, 4] 
   and [5, 6, 7] and place your {5} to make it [2, 3, 4, 5] and [5, 6, 7]

   You can also merge packs to further change it. eg: you have {red 9} and {orange 9} on board: [black 4, 5, 6] and [black 7, 8 , 9].
   merge to make [black 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9] and then take the {9} to make [red, orange, black 9 pack] and [black 4, 5, 6, 7, 8 pack]
   
   You can replace a card with one of the same value which is redundant as you are left with the same card which you cannot add to your 
   deck as it has been already placed

      However, this becomes useful with jokers. eg: you have {black 5} and {blue 10} and {blue 11}, board has [black 4, joker, 6],
      you can replace the joker with the {black 5} and use the joker with your other cards to make [black 4, 5, 6 pack] and
      [blue 10, 11, joker]
